1
00:00:00,949 --> 00:00:04,449
(Gablehouser:)Today's preliminary match
features two great teams:

2
00:00:04,911 --> 00:00:09,791
(Gablehouser:)AA versus PMS.

3
00:00:09,958 --> 00:00:11,958
(Howard:)All night long, y'all.

4
00:00:16,422 --> 00:00:19,552
(Gablehouser:)Okay, well, let's jump right in.
First question.

5
00:00:19,717 --> 00:00:25,057
For 10 points. "What is the isospin
singlet partner of the pi-zero meson?"

6
00:00:25,223 --> 00:00:26,303
[BUZZER SOUNDS]

7
00:00:26,474 --> 00:00:28,304
- PMS?
- The eta meson.

8
00:00:28,476 --> 00:00:29,766
(Penny:)Correct.

9
00:00:31,646 --> 00:00:33,226
- Formal protest.
- On what grounds?

10
00:00:33,398 --> 00:00:36,528
(Sheldon:)The Velcro on my wrist brace
caught on my shirt.

11
00:00:36,693 --> 00:00:39,653
Denied. All right, for 10 points.

12
00:00:39,821 --> 00:00:43,701
"What is the lightest element on Earth
with no stable isotope?"

13
00:00:43,867 --> 00:00:44,997
[BUZZER SOUNDS]

14
00:00:45,159 --> 00:00:47,249
(Leonard:)- AA?
- And, of course, the answer is technetium.

15
00:00:47,412 --> 00:00:49,122
(Gablehouser:)Terrific.

16
00:00:49,497 --> 00:00:53,087
Next question. "What is the force
between two uncharged plates...

17
00:00:53,251 --> 00:00:55,081
...due to quantum vacuum fluctuation?"

18
00:00:55,253 --> 00:00:56,293
[BUZZER SOUNDS]

19
00:00:56,462 --> 00:00:58,002
- PMS?
- And Sheldon can suck on...

20
00:00:58,172 --> 00:01:05,022
(Raj:)- ...the Casimir effect.
GABLEHAUSER: Correct.

